 4. 👟 5-borough marathon turns 50 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Bill Rodgers, of Melrose, Mass., crosses the finish line to win the New York City Marathon in 1976. Photo: AP In 1976, the New York City Marathon ran through all five boroughs for the first time.

 There were just over 2,000 competitors in that seventh running of the race, including only 88 women. This morning, about 60,000 runners stepped up to the starting line, nearly half of them women. Go deeper . 

 
 
