 7. ☎️ Modern landline 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: Tin Can Parents who want to avoid smartphones are buying old-school phones so their kids can chat with friends, Axios San Diego's Claire Trageser reports . 

 Case in point: Tin Can, a $100 retro-style phone that runs on Wi-Fi, lets kids call only parent-approved numbers.

 Other companies offer similar products, including Pinwheel Home, Ooma MyPhone, Wiley Buddy, Ring Ring Club and Voiply's Kids Phone Plan. Why can't you just get a landline?

 It's not that easy: Getting a traditional copper-wire connection has become harder. Plus, phones like Tin Can that ring for only approved numbers block spam calls. Keep reading ... Get Axios Local . 

 
 
