 8. 🏀 1 for the road: WNBA champ 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Golden State Valkyries forward Gabby Williams (right) jumps for a shot while Atlanta Dream forward DeWanna Bonner blocks. Photo: Stephen Lam/San Francisco Chronicle via Getty Images The Golden State Valkyries, led by Gabby Williams , survived a back-and-forth Game 7 battle to beat the Atlanta Dream 68-63 and win the 2026 WNBA Championship in the Valkyries' second season as a franchise. 

 Williams, who scored 30 points in front of last night's violet-clad crowd at Chase Center in San Francisco, was named the 2026 WNBA Finals MVP. Photo: Ina Fried/Axios Ina Fried, Axios' chief tech correspondent, takes a selfie with the Golden State Valkyries mascot, Violet — a raven who goes by Vi.

